# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Generated templ code (regenerate with `go generate ./...`)
*_templ.go

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
 .idea/
# .vscode/
pkg/account/client/
!pkg/account/client/mocks/
.aider*
*.md
!AGENTS.md
!README.md
!docs/*.md
pinner
completions/
.sisyphus/
# The Sunpeak MCP e2e fixture HOME contains a pinner config.yaml; re-include
# that config dir so the suite's sealed config (pointing at cmd/mcp-test-server)
# ships with the repo. The bare `pinner` rule above would otherwise swallow
# this path as an ignored directory.
!tests/sunpeak/fixtures/pinner-home/.config/pinner/
# fake API boot log emitted by the globalSetup harness
tests/sunpeak/.mcp-e2e-fake.log

# Git worktrees
.worktrees/

# Scratch diagnostic scripts (live e2e checks); not part of the build
docs/mcp_e2e_check.py

# Node / pnpm workspace (JS app bundle build; never published)
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
**/dist/

# ...except the MCP Apps embedded bundles, which ARE committed/released as the
# published artifact: the importable mcpapp package ships them via go:embed so
# a hosted composition root (e.g. the Portal MCP plugin) can render ui:// app
# views from the module alone. Regenerated by the `make assets` jsbuild step.
!mcpapp/appsassets/dist/
!mcpapp/appsassets/dist/*.js

# The compiled MCP Apps Tailwind theme (mcpapp/css/tailwind.css) and the
# generated mcpcanvas AssetSource manifest (mcpapp/appsassets/manifest.json)
# are committed/released like the dist bundles above: they are the published
# importable mcpapp artifact, regenerated by `make cssbuild` / genappmanifest
# and kept in sync with the source assets.

# Sunpeak / Playwright MCP test artifacts
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright/
tests/evals/.env
.auth/
bin/


# MCP Apps JS build / local tooling artifacts
# (no trailing slash: also ignore the worktree symlinks to shared caches)
node_modules
.venv
